1
00:00:13,230 --> 00:00:15,571
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what would you say if somebody asked you how to be mindful?

2
00:00:15,891 --> 00:00:17,331
[SPEAKER_00]: How to sustain in mindfulness?

3
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:20,732
[SPEAKER_00]: How to carry on being mindful?

4
00:00:20,932 --> 00:00:26,913
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like you must be mindful, then you're mindful when you remember to be mindful, but then you lapse, you forget.

5
00:00:27,013 --> 00:00:29,694
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how would you... how to sustain mindfulness?

6
00:00:36,335 --> 00:00:39,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, if you know what mindfulness is, then you can sustain it.

7
00:00:39,796 --> 00:00:39,976
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

8
00:00:40,056 --> 00:00:43,097
[SPEAKER_00]: So, already, if you have a right direction,

9
00:00:44,638 --> 00:00:45,418
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what would then...

10
00:00:47,059 --> 00:00:47,900
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how would you sustain it?

11
00:00:49,621 --> 00:00:51,362
[SPEAKER_00]: How would you know what it is in order to sustain it?

12
00:00:52,563 --> 00:00:55,966
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, you need to know what you...

13
00:00:56,026 --> 00:00:57,527
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to be mindful of what?

14
00:00:58,027 --> 00:01:01,430
[SPEAKER_01]: Mindful of, let's say, of the body.

15
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:02,770
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

16
00:01:02,831 --> 00:01:03,151
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah.

17
00:01:03,171 --> 00:01:04,792
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you need something to be mindful of.

18
00:01:06,626 --> 00:01:16,354
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what would be the difference between being mindful of the body and being mindful of this, I don't know, roof above my head?

19
00:01:19,717 --> 00:01:21,979
[SPEAKER_00]: Being mindful of the body and being mindful of my hands.

20
00:01:22,899 --> 00:01:25,722
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the difference?

21
00:01:25,742 --> 00:01:28,664
[SPEAKER_01]: The extension, I guess.

22
00:01:29,585 --> 00:01:30,626
[SPEAKER_01]: The thing that you're placing.

23
00:01:30,993 --> 00:01:33,275
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, how specific or how general it is.

24
00:01:33,375 --> 00:01:34,456
[SPEAKER_01]: But the roof is not your...

25
00:01:34,597 --> 00:01:35,237
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, the roof is not...

26
00:01:35,257 --> 00:01:35,678
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can.

27
00:01:35,698 --> 00:01:38,821
[SPEAKER_00]: I can be mindful of the roof if I'm worried that something will fall on the roof and destroy it.

28
00:01:38,921 --> 00:01:41,003
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I am very mindful of what's happening to the roof.

29
00:01:41,243 --> 00:01:41,443
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

30
00:01:42,024 --> 00:01:42,825
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's the difference.

31
00:01:42,845 --> 00:01:51,233
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, whether it's a specific thing or whether you have something that's more, like, fundamental to your experience, such as your body, your feeling, the whole...

32
00:01:51,253 --> 00:01:53,315
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I could be mindful if I'm doing work here.

33
00:01:55,772 --> 00:01:59,835
[SPEAKER_01]: That's... and this... this roof might fall down.

34
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:00,415
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

35
00:02:00,796 --> 00:02:03,157
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I'm mindful of that roof.

36
00:02:03,217 --> 00:02:03,537
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

37
00:02:03,557 --> 00:02:09,081
[SPEAKER_01]: That context that whatever I'm doing here is subject to... Because you're under it, yeah.

38
00:02:09,682 --> 00:02:13,384
[SPEAKER_00]: But why is then being mindful of your body better than being mindful of the roof?

39
00:02:13,905 --> 00:02:14,865
[SPEAKER_00]: Why would that be better?

40
00:02:15,906 --> 00:02:17,767
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there's a different goal, I suppose.

41
00:02:18,328 --> 00:02:21,110
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that and because it already includes mindfulness of the roof.

42
00:02:21,976 --> 00:02:23,577
[SPEAKER_00]: See, if you're under the roof, they might fall.

43
00:02:23,617 --> 00:02:29,141
[SPEAKER_00]: If you're mindful of your body, you're already mindful of the danger of it being crushed by the roof or anything other than the roof.

44
00:02:30,062 --> 00:02:34,065
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you're mindful of the roof, anything else that's higher than that, you won't be mindful of.

45
00:02:34,565 --> 00:02:40,370
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's at least the mindfulness... the points for recollection, points for mindfulness are the reference points.

46
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:42,571
[SPEAKER_00]: But it matters what reference point.

47
00:02:44,212 --> 00:02:47,115
[SPEAKER_00]: So, not like, oh, I'm mindful of pleasure that I'm chasing.

48
00:02:47,515 --> 00:02:50,057
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you're mindful of feeling, but that's not mindfulness of feeling.

49
00:02:50,941 --> 00:02:55,764
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to be mindful of feeling in the general sense that includes every other particular feeling you might be going through.

50
00:02:56,184 --> 00:02:58,485
[SPEAKER_00]: So, mindful of the nature that you're subjected to feeling.

51
00:03:00,447 --> 00:03:04,969
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, mindful of the body is there, regardless of whether it's at risk of this or something else.

52
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:17,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that reveals then the whole scope of what that body is subjected to, not just the particular danger of the roof and the non-danger if you step outside of the possibly imminently falling roof.

53
00:03:19,331 --> 00:03:23,235
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever you're doing, you're mindful of the context of body.

54
00:03:23,255 --> 00:03:25,597
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's... we always kind of end up revolving around context.

55
00:03:25,697 --> 00:03:30,301
[SPEAKER_00]: You are already in the... your body already gives you the... provides you the basis for the context you're in.

56
00:03:31,843 --> 00:03:33,004
[SPEAKER_01]: So, just not forgetting.

57
00:03:33,624 --> 00:03:35,166
[SPEAKER_00]: Not... Yeah.

58
00:03:35,186 --> 00:03:36,647
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how would you then not forget?

59
00:03:36,827 --> 00:03:37,888
[SPEAKER_00]: That is, how do you sustain?

60
00:03:38,089 --> 00:03:39,030
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you would still lapse.

61
00:03:40,091 --> 00:03:42,132
[SPEAKER_00]: So, we want to basically understand why you lapse.

62
00:03:42,895 --> 00:03:43,776
[SPEAKER_00]: And how not to lapse?

63
00:03:44,436 --> 00:03:45,817
[SPEAKER_00]: From the context that is there.

64
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:50,859
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you lapse from your mindfulness, you haven't lapsed from the body that's subjected to all these things.

65
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:55,422
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you then... you can't change the body and what's subjected to.

66
00:03:56,042 --> 00:04:00,344
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, it's only because of stuff you do, that you get to lapse from what's obvious.

67
00:04:01,365 --> 00:04:03,026
[SPEAKER_01]: So, remembering the context.

68
00:04:03,106 --> 00:04:04,426
[SPEAKER_01]: You're asking how to remember the context.

69
00:04:04,447 --> 00:04:10,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, and then refraining from doing things that basically are contradicting the context, that are countering, that are against it.

70
00:04:12,619 --> 00:04:17,941
[SPEAKER_00]: The context of that, like, oh, this body is subjected to this whole vast scope domain of things that I cannot even fathom.

71
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:19,141
[SPEAKER_00]: And you feel that.

72
00:04:20,041 --> 00:04:24,623
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, if you ignore it, and it's, oh, a roof is a danger, I avoid the roof, thus I am safe.

73
00:04:25,283 --> 00:04:27,404
[SPEAKER_00]: And you ignore the fact that that's only a relative safety.

74
00:04:28,724 --> 00:04:30,425
[SPEAKER_00]: A relative sort of ease.

75
00:04:31,225 --> 00:04:38,207
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you kind of reconnect with the notion, yeah, but the body is still there, depends on organs, depends on the elements, so there's no safety there.

76
00:04:39,568 --> 00:04:40,488
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's unpleasant now.

77
00:04:41,837 --> 00:04:48,742
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't want this pleasure, so I'll just selectively kind of pick on and establish my mind upon safety.

78
00:04:48,882 --> 00:04:49,602
[SPEAKER_00]: Relative safety.

79
00:04:50,523 --> 00:04:52,224
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why you lapse from mindfulness.

80
00:04:52,424 --> 00:04:55,486
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you choose to ignore the context because it's unpleasant at times.

81
00:04:55,907 --> 00:04:59,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Not always, but at times it's unpleasant and you don't want it.

82
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:02,791
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you want to sustain the mindfulness?

83
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:04,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop trying to avoid this pleasure.

84
00:05:07,514 --> 00:05:08,335
[SPEAKER_00]: Pretty much of any kind.

85
00:05:10,267 --> 00:05:16,948
[SPEAKER_00]: Not torture yourself, but when unpleasant feelings manifest, stop trying to justify it, outrun it, explain it, get rid of it.

86
00:05:17,328 --> 00:05:18,569
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to allow it to endure.

87
00:05:19,949 --> 00:05:22,169
[SPEAKER_00]: And by the way, that's another way you could easily be mindful of it.

88
00:05:22,309 --> 00:05:24,430
[SPEAKER_00]: Effortlessly be mindful of the context.

89
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:26,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Find something deeply concerning.

90
00:05:29,631 --> 00:05:34,712
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the whole life revolves around avoiding concerns, covering them up, dealing with them, literally.

91
00:05:37,093 --> 00:05:39,153
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's always a concern in the back of your mind.

92
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:43,771
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's obviously a bit edgy, because it can overwhelm you.

93
00:05:46,832 --> 00:05:48,712
[SPEAKER_01]: So, finding a concern.

94
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:49,152
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

95
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:52,433
[SPEAKER_01]: Something, so, I'm concerned of losing something.

96
00:05:52,613 --> 00:05:54,293
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, find that and then work through that.

97
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:55,093
[SPEAKER_00]: Something might change.

98
00:05:55,454 --> 00:06:06,316
[SPEAKER_00]: And you don't need to see, like, when there is a concern present in your experience, the effort is not... never is on the level of, oh, I need to keep this concern, otherwise I'll forget about it.

99
00:06:06,716 --> 00:06:08,717
[SPEAKER_00]: No, the effort is, I must forget about this.

100
00:06:08,817 --> 00:06:09,677
[SPEAKER_00]: I must outrun it.

101
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:15,865
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you find a concern, you will be unable to forget about it.

102
00:06:17,388 --> 00:06:17,808
[SPEAKER_01]: Unless you...

103
00:06:17,868 --> 00:06:21,734
[SPEAKER_00]: Unless you intentionally make this excess effort to cover it up.

104
00:06:21,774 --> 00:06:27,382
[SPEAKER_00]: So, remember what you're concerned... Yeah, so, like, basically, dig up the concern, or as the Buddha would say, sense of urgency.

105
00:06:29,015 --> 00:06:31,096
[SPEAKER_00]: And that will effortlessly stay there.

106
00:06:31,836 --> 00:06:41,140
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need effort, because if you just take mindfulness on your own terms, I'm mindful now, you need all this effort to keep that mindfulness going, because this is gonna fade, because it's not really the mindfulness-mindfulness.

107
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:46,842
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not based on the context you're in, it's the context that you kind of scraped up, thinking that's what the context I'm in.

108
00:06:48,815 --> 00:06:53,998
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you find a concern, you'll never intentionally scrape up the concern and enjoy it to be there.

109
00:06:54,398 --> 00:07:00,041
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what's concerning about the body is... You don't even need to start specifically about concern of the body.

110
00:07:00,121 --> 00:07:05,504
[SPEAKER_00]: Just any concern, any unease that you have, and then...

111
00:07:05,604 --> 00:07:06,825
[SPEAKER_00]: Allow that thought to endure.

112
00:07:07,185 --> 00:07:09,066
[SPEAKER_00]: You are mindful of the body there.

113
00:07:09,866 --> 00:07:11,127
[SPEAKER_00]: You're mindful of the feeling there.

114
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,532
[SPEAKER_01]: You're mindful of the danger in the body.

115
00:07:14,713 --> 00:07:16,434
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it becomes very apparent, yeah.

116
00:07:16,995 --> 00:07:20,739
[SPEAKER_00]: So, as I said, the only effort that you would be making would not be effort.

117
00:07:20,799 --> 00:07:24,162
[SPEAKER_00]: I must stay mindful, because you are mindful, because the concern will endure effortlessly.

118
00:07:24,943 --> 00:07:33,552
[SPEAKER_00]: The only effort you will be making, and thus restraining yourself from making it, if you want to practice mindfulness, is effort for distracting yourself from that concerned mindfulness.

119
00:07:36,003 --> 00:07:36,623
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's easier.

120
00:07:37,163 --> 00:07:37,584
[SPEAKER_00]: It's clear.

121
00:07:38,444 --> 00:07:41,505
[SPEAKER_00]: As you said, you can't be mindful because you don't know what mindfulness is.

122
00:07:42,245 --> 00:07:46,026
[SPEAKER_00]: And now you know exactly what will take you away from this concern, and you choose to not do it.

123
00:07:47,046 --> 00:07:48,747
[SPEAKER_00]: Because then you will lose your mindfulness.

124
00:07:50,848 --> 00:07:53,348
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's a little recognition of I am prey to suffering.

125
00:07:54,249 --> 00:07:55,209
[SPEAKER_00]: And you cannot shake it off.

126
00:07:55,749 --> 00:07:57,350
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's literally... that's your situation.

127
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,130
[SPEAKER_00]: It's unshakable.

128
00:07:59,571 --> 00:08:03,733
[SPEAKER_00]: The only way people can shake it off is cover it up, which we don't want to shake it off.

129
00:08:03,793 --> 00:08:07,614
[SPEAKER_00]: They just put a bandage on the wound, so they don't... not to treat the wound, but not to see the wound.

130
00:08:08,955 --> 00:08:12,596
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just make up, so you don't see that the wound is still very much there.

131
00:08:16,418 --> 00:08:22,721
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it doesn't need to be some great concern that you cannot possibly cope with, but you certainly need to start digging them up, because they are there.

132
00:08:23,361 --> 00:08:25,622
[SPEAKER_00]: Most people's lives revolve around avoiding anxiety,

133
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,162
[SPEAKER_00]: And trying to basically prevent it from arising.

134
00:08:29,422 --> 00:08:38,789
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, if your situation is not already deeply anxious, as a human being, you wouldn't be experiencing anxiety to begin with.

135
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:41,451
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just a revelation of what your situation already is.

136
00:08:43,182 --> 00:08:49,127
[SPEAKER_00]: And that kind of breeds the whole kind of dependence on centrality and the whole constant movement, constant activity, constant projects.

137
00:08:49,467 --> 00:08:53,030
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if I stop, I settle back into my situation.

138
00:08:53,210 --> 00:08:54,811
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's already the beginning of mindfulness.

139
00:08:55,152 --> 00:08:58,614
[SPEAKER_00]: So you realize most people lose mindfulness is because deep down they don't want to be mindful.

140
00:08:59,475 --> 00:09:05,100
[SPEAKER_00]: They want to do mindfulness on their own terms, but they don't want to be mindful because that reveals this... oh...

141
00:09:05,842 --> 00:09:10,707
[SPEAKER_00]: The nature of my situation, it's subject to change, subject to all these things that will be on... That's frightening.

142
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:13,851
[SPEAKER_00]: Frightening from the point of view of my assumed change and control.

143
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:16,453
[SPEAKER_00]: Not frightening in itself.

144
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:19,216
[SPEAKER_00]: If you get used to it, the fear will go away.

145
00:09:21,319 --> 00:09:22,500
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a right concern.

146
00:09:23,411 --> 00:09:24,692
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, we actually spoke about it, didn't we?

147
00:09:24,712 --> 00:09:25,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, we did.

148
00:09:25,113 --> 00:09:26,554
[SPEAKER_00]: We had a whole talk on the right concern.

149
00:09:26,574 --> 00:09:28,015
[SPEAKER_01]: That was like the prerequisite.

150
00:09:28,035 --> 00:09:28,856
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, that's it.

151
00:09:28,896 --> 00:09:29,216
[SPEAKER_00]: There it is.

152
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:29,837
[SPEAKER_00]: Right concern.

153
00:09:29,997 --> 00:09:32,099
[SPEAKER_00]: I didn't have it in mind when we started, but that's exactly what it is, yeah.

154
00:09:32,199 --> 00:09:33,640
[SPEAKER_01]: The right concern will result out of it.

155
00:09:34,221 --> 00:09:35,762
[SPEAKER_00]: So, right concern, right mindfulness.

156
00:09:35,802 --> 00:09:37,043
[SPEAKER_01]: Right mindfulness, right concern.

157
00:09:38,885 --> 00:09:42,689
[SPEAKER_00]: And right mindfulness, as the Buddha said, it's where you can't have too much of it.

158
00:09:44,590 --> 00:09:46,892
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't overdo your situation.

159
00:09:47,113 --> 00:09:49,635
[SPEAKER_00]: You can just be more clearer and clearer about it.

160
00:09:50,949 --> 00:10:03,338
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you're clear about, to the extent necessary, you will have uprooted any misconstrued notions and assumptions about the nature of what you're subjected to, the nature of anicca, nature of change, that whole thing.

161
00:10:04,517 --> 00:10:17,462
[SPEAKER_00]: The only reason you carry on these gratuitous assumptions and sense of ownership and my and I am, is because you really, like, you maintain it through refusing to address the basic characteristics of your situation.

162
00:10:17,702 --> 00:10:21,343
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I just, say, be mindful of the body,

163
00:10:22,728 --> 00:10:26,430
[SPEAKER_01]: Without seeing... having no concern over it.

164
00:10:26,610 --> 00:10:27,711
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it's going to be mechanical.

165
00:10:28,251 --> 00:10:28,671
[SPEAKER_00]: It's going to be...

166
00:10:28,691 --> 00:10:29,151
[SPEAKER_00]: It's kind of boring.

167
00:10:29,311 --> 00:10:29,952
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, boring.

168
00:10:30,012 --> 00:10:32,693
[SPEAKER_00]: It might be... And that's exactly why you won't be able to sustain it.

169
00:10:32,713 --> 00:10:34,414
[SPEAKER_00]: That's exactly why you need more... No, no, no.

170
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,835
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not mindfulness of the body.

171
00:10:35,915 --> 00:10:37,956
[SPEAKER_00]: That's mindfulness of what you assume body to be.

172
00:10:39,192 --> 00:10:39,692
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I mean.

173
00:10:39,712 --> 00:10:42,835
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, if you do mindfulness rightly, you... it's not... it's not your doing.

174
00:10:43,235 --> 00:10:44,656
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just discerning what's already there.

175
00:10:44,996 --> 00:10:48,018
[SPEAKER_00]: That's exactly why mindfulness results in culmination of knowledge.

176
00:10:48,639 --> 00:10:50,380
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, of understanding.

177
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:52,342
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to see the danger in the body.

178
00:10:53,002 --> 00:10:53,863
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have to... That's it.

179
00:10:54,123 --> 00:11:00,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Seeing the danger of the body is actually more aligned with mindfulness of the body than you being mindful of the body.

180
00:11:02,266 --> 00:11:05,768
[SPEAKER_00]: When you do that, oh, I'm mindful of the body now, you know, I'm feeling this chair and whatever else.

181
00:11:05,788 --> 00:11:08,270
[SPEAKER_01]: Because once you grasp the danger... That's already the body.

182
00:11:08,290 --> 00:11:11,512
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not going to be... you're going to have one eye open, so to speak.

183
00:11:11,532 --> 00:11:11,752
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah.

184
00:11:11,912 --> 00:11:12,792
[SPEAKER_01]: You're already alert.

185
00:11:13,013 --> 00:11:13,213
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

186
00:11:13,293 --> 00:11:15,094
[SPEAKER_01]: You're going to be alert, heedful, so to speak.

187
00:11:15,214 --> 00:11:22,498
[SPEAKER_00]: So, people want to be alert and heedful on their own terms, without feeling the pang of that anxiety and danger.

188
00:11:22,999 --> 00:11:24,860
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's then not alertness, isn't it?

189
00:11:27,741 --> 00:11:28,502
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, alert to what?

190
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:31,282
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, no, but this is still alertness.

191
